# QikLog — project rules

Operating context for any AI assistant working in this repo.

## What QikLog is

A lightweight log-tailing SaaS for developers who want to see what their app is doing in real time without setting up Datadog or Grafana. Indie/.NET-first positioning. The product is "tail -f from a browser, but also a CLI, also an SDK."

## Stack

- **.NET 9 LTS** for everything (Core, Api, Web, Cli)
- **ASP.NET Core minimal APIs** for `QikLog.Api`
- **SignalR** for real-time log streaming (not raw SSE — we use SignalR for built-in reconnect, grouping, and Blazor symmetry)
- **Blazor Server** + **Fluent UI Blazor** for the dashboard (`QikLog.Web`)
- **System.CommandLine** for the CLI (`QikLog.Cli`), published as a single-file self-contained executable
- **PostgreSQL 16** for persistent storage (Phase 2+)
- **Redis 7** for hot buffers, rate limiting, SignalR backplane when scaling (Phase 2+)
- **Docker Compose** for local dev
- **xUnit + Shouldly** for tests
- **GitHub Actions** for CI
- **Azure Container Apps** for production hosting (Phase 4+)

## Project layout

- `src/QikLog.Core/` — domain models, validation, contracts. Reference target for everything else. No web/IO dependencies.
- `src/QikLog.Api/` — minimal API + SignalR `LogHub`. Stateless except for in-memory state during MVP.
- `src/QikLog.Web/` — Blazor Server dashboard. Uses SignalR client to subscribe to `LogHub`.
- `src/QikLog.Cli/` — `qiklog send`, `qiklog tail-file`, more later.
- `tests/QikLog.Core.Tests/` — unit tests; add API/Web test projects as those grow.

## Coding conventions

- File-scoped namespaces always.
- `sealed` by default on classes and records — open them only when there's a real reason.
- Records for DTOs and value objects; classes for entities with identity.
- Nullable reference types enabled and warnings as errors. Don't suppress with `!` unless there's a comment explaining why.
- Use primary constructors and collection expressions (C# 12/13 features) freely.
- `var` is fine when the type is obvious from the right-hand side; explicit type when it aids readability.
- Async all the way down. No `.Result` or `.Wait()`. Pass `CancellationToken` through every async call.
- DI via constructor injection. No service locator pattern.
- Logging via `ILogger<T>`. Structured logging with named placeholders, never string interpolation:
  - Good: `_log.LogInformation("Ingested {Count} entries for {Source}", count, source);`
  - Bad: `_log.LogInformation($"Ingested {count} entries for {source}");`
- Tests use `Shouldly` for assertions (`result.ShouldBe(expected)`), not `Assert.Equal`.

## Naming

- Public API surface: `PascalCase`, no Hungarian, no `I` prefix on records.
- Private fields: `_camelCase` with leading underscore.
- SignalR groups: `source:{name}` convention. Keep names grep-able.
- Configuration keys: `QikLog:Section:Key` in `appsettings.json`, `QikLog__Section__Key` as env vars.

## What we are NOT building right now

When suggesting code, do not add:
- Authentication / authorization (coming Phase 2)
- Multi-tenancy enforcement (coming Phase 2)
- Persistence beyond in-memory (coming Phase 2)
- Alerts / webhooks (Phase 3)
- Billing / Stripe (Phase 4)
- Agents in other languages (Phase 2+)

If a task seems to need one of those, flag it and ask before scaffolding it in. Premature scope creep is the enemy.

## Brand

The visual identity is the **terminal Q with a blinking cursor**. Accent color is teal (`#2dd4bf` on dark, `#0d9488` on light). Wordmark is `qiklog` in monospace with `log` in the accent color and a blinking cursor block trailing the `g`.

**Never hardcode hex values in components.** All colors live as CSS custom properties in `src/QikLog.Web/wwwroot/brand/brand.css`. Reference them as `var(--ql-accent-teal)`, `var(--ql-surface-ink)`, etc. If you need a color that isn't there, add it to `brand.css` as a new `--ql-*` token first, then use it. This keeps the brand tunable from one file.

Brand assets live in `src/QikLog.Web/wwwroot/brand/`:
- `icon.svg` — animated icon (cursor blinks)
- `favicon.svg` — static favicon
- `lockup.svg` — icon + wordmark for headers/READMEs
- `brand.css` — all design tokens
- See `docs/BRAND_GUIDE.md` for the full guide.

The logo is a prototype. Treat it as good enough to ship the MVP, not as the final mark. A designer pass comes after $1K MRR.

## Commits

Use Conventional Commits. Format: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`.

Types: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert.
Scopes: api, web, cli, core, infra, brand, deps. Omit if it spans multiple.
Description: lowercase, imperative ("add" not "added"), no trailing period.

Examples:
- `feat(api): add POST /v1/logs ingest endpoint`
- `fix(web): reconnect SignalR hub on transient drop`
- `chore(deps): bump FluentUI to 4.12.0`
- `refactor(core): extract LogEntry validation into rules`
- `docs(brand): document cursor blink animation rhythm`

Breaking changes: append `!` to type and add `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
Reference issues with `Closes #N` or `Refs #N` in the footer.

Prefer small commits. If you wrote "and" in the description, it should have been two commits.
